    { version = "2.3.0", text = "Radial Menu opening options, chat link tooltips, and more control over how every unit frame looks.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Radial Menu: |cffffffffMenu position|r (Options tab): open radials at your mouse cursor (the default) or in the middle of the screen. Radial macros open there too.\n• Radial Menu: |cffffffffActivation|r (Options tab): |cffffffffHold|r (as before: hold the key, point, release) or |cffffffffToggle|r: press the key to open the radial and keep it open. Left-click or press the key again uses the slice you point at, right-click goes back a level or closes, Escape closes. Middle-click a nested radial to open it in place of the current one; the mouse wheel still steps through it.\n• Chat: |cffffffffLink tooltips on hover|r (Tweaks, on by default): point at an item, spell or quest link in chat to see its tooltip, without clicking.\n• Unit Frames: |cffffffffBackground Opacity|r at the end of Look in Edit Mode, on every unit frame (player, target, focus, pet, player cast bar, target of target, target of focus, party, raid and boss): how dark the empty part of the bars is, from 0% to 100%. Cast bars follow their frame's setting.\n• Unit Frames: |cffffffffFull Player Names|r (Look, on by default): players' first names and surnames on every unit frame. Off shows the first name only.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Unit Frames: |cffffffffBorder Texture|r is now on every frame in FlareUI Style and Addon Style, the player, target and focus frames included. Forever Style has no border options at all: its border is fixed on every frame.\n• Unit Frames: the level of a friendly unit (anything you can't attack) shows in Blizzard's gold, in every style. Enemies keep the difficulty colours.\n• Bar and border dropdowns: FlareUI's own options come first, then a line and the bars or borders other addons add, A-Z. LibSharedMedia's built-in Blizzard bars and borders are no longer listed.\n• FlareUI's options in those dropdowns: FlareUI Thick and FlareUI Thin for Border Texture; None and FlareUI Frames for the Chat, Damage Meter and Quest Tracker borders; FlareUI Flat, FlareUI Forever and FlareUI Striped for Bar, Cast Bar and Absorb Texture. A frame already set to something no longer listed keeps it.\n• |cffffffffFrame Texture|r is gone from Cast Bar Texture and Absorb Texture." },
    { version = "2.2.1", text = "|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Target and focus frames: switching straight from one target to another no longer leaves the last target's debuffs on the frame. They showed up as duplicates, and their timers sat at 0 or were missing (reported in a dungeon). Party, boss and raid frames get the same fix when a new unit takes a frame (a new boss, a roster change).\n• Target and focus frames: |cffffffffOnly My Debuffs|r now shows only the debuffs you cast. Before, it showed every player's debuffs." },
    { version = "2.2.0", text = "Improvements from your feedback: whole-width aura rows, cast bars that make room for auras, tooltip level colours and a tidier minimap.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Unit Frames: buffs and debuffs can go |cffffffffTop|r or |cffffffffBottom|r, across the frame's whole width. Party and boss frames get |cffffffffAbove the Frame|r, |cffffffffBelow the Frame|r, |cffffffffInside, Top|r and |cffffffffInside, Bottom|r. A whole-width place greys out the other places on that edge for the other kind of aura.\n• Tooltips: the target's level is coloured by difficulty against yours (grey, green, yellow, orange, red), as quests are.\n• Minimap: a |cffffffffFonts|r tab for the zone name and the clock.\n• Minimap: drag and drop the buttons in the addon button drawer to reorder them. The order is kept, and new addons go last.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Target, focus, party and boss frames: auras sit right against the frame. The cast bar shows next to the frame and, while it shows, pushes the auras on its side out past it; they come back when the cast ends.\n• Party frames: |cffffffffLeft of the Frame|r is gone from the aura places, and boss frames lose |cffffffffRight of the Frame|r. Auras set there move to the other side." },
